; A prefix key bound to completion:narrow-key-keymap in
; completion:narrowing-keymap narrows by the next character and keeps the
; input, as consult-narrow does; a character no source has, such as the
; prefix again, widens. A read with no narrow characters lacks the
; prefix, which types itself there.
> (keys:bind! completion:narrowing-keymap "<" completion:narrow-key-keymap)
